slides.content:
# Slide In from the Side

An off‑canvas menu sits off‑screen (e.g., `transform: translateX(-100%)`) and slides in when toggled. It overlays or pushes the main content. CSS `transition` provides the animation.

Key CSS:
```css
.offcanvas {
  position: fixed;
  top: 0; left: 0;
  width: 80%; height: 100%;
  background: white;
  transform: translateX(-100%);
  transition: transform 0.3s;
}
.offcanvas.open {
  transform: translateX(0);
}
```
Accessibility: trap focus inside the menu when open, add a close button, and use `aria-hidden`.
